{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(x1) >= 0 ∧ dtype_(x1) <= 8 ∧ dtype_(x2) >= 0 ∧ dtype_(x2) <= 8 ) ∨ shape(x1) ≠ shape(x2)
>>
Rule 95 (if one is bool then other must be bool and shape must be equal)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(x1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(x2) = 0 then (dtype_(x1) = 0 ∧ dtype_(x2) = 0 ∧ shape(x1) = shape(x2))
>>
Rule 96 (If both tensors have at least one dimension, and number of dimensions are same then all dimensions must have same length shape.)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(x1) > 0) ∧ (ndim(x2) > 0) ∧ (ndim(x1) = ndim(x2)) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x1) - 1]: shape(x1,i) = shape(x2, i))
>>
Rule 97 (If tensor is boolean and has at least one dimension, all the shape dimension must be of same length)
{x1 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(x1) = 0) ∧ (ndim(x1) > 0) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x1) - 1]: shape(x1, i) = shape(x1, 0))
>>
Rule 98 (If one shape of the tensors dimension is 1 all others must be one)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(x1) - 1] : shape(x1, i) = 1 then ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(x1) - 1] : shape(x1, j) = 1 else if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(x2) - 1] : shape(x2, i) = 1 then ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(x2) - 1] : shape(x2, j) = 1
>>
Rule 99 (If the number of dimensions are not same for both tensors then one tensor has to be a scalar with the dtype of a bool)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(x1) ≠ ndim(x2)) then (ndim(x1) = 0 ∧ dtype_(x1) = 0) ∨ (ndim(x2) = 0 ∧ dtype_(x2) = 0)
>>
Rule 100 (if shapes of both tensors are not equal then their dtypes should be from different categories (boolean, integer, float, complex).)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if shape(x1) ≠ shape(x2) then (dtype_(x1) <= 0 ∧ dtype_(x2) > 0) ∨ (dtype_(x2) <= 0 ∧ dtype_(x1) > 0)
>>
Rule 101 (If the number of dimension of the tensors are the same, then both dtypes must be in the same family)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(x1) = ndim(x2) ∧ ndim(x1) > 0 ∧ ndim(x2) > 0) then (dtype_(x1) <= 0 ∧ dtype_(x2) <= 0) ∨ ((dtype_(x1) >= 1 ∧ dtype_(x1) <= 8) ∧ (dtype_(x2) >= 1 ∧ dtype_(x2) <= 8)) ∨ ((dtype_(x1) >= 9 ∧ dtype_(x1) <= 10) ∧ (dtype_(x2) >= 9 ∧ dtype_(x2) <= 10))
>>
Rule 103 (If both dtypes are equal and numeric then number of dim should be equal)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(x1) >= 1 ∧ dtype_(x1) <= 8) ∧ (dtype_(x2) >= 1 ∧ dtype_(x2) <= 8) ∧ (dtype_(x1) = dtype_(x2)) then ndim(x1) = ndim(x2)
>>
Rule 104 (If the two tensors have same shape then both data type families should also be the same.)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if shape(x1) = shape(x2) then (dtype_(x1) <= 0 ∧ dtype_(x2) <= 0) ∨ ((dtype_(x1) >= 1 ∧ dtype_(x1) <= 8) ∧ (dtype_(x2) >= 1 ∧ dtype_(x2) <= 8)) ∨ ((dtype_(x1) >= 9 ∧ dtype_(x1) <= 10) ∧ (dtype_(x2) >= 9 ∧ dtype_(x2) <= 10))
>>
Rule 105 (Tensors must be either boolean or must support comparison)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(x1) = 0 ∧ dtype_(x2) = 0) ∨ (dtype_(x1) >= 1 ∧ dtype_(x1) <= 10) ∧ (dtype_(x2) >= 1 ∧ dtype_(x2) <= 10)
